---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig, CANONICAL_PERSON_ID } from '../config/site';

const title = 'Methodology & How Tools Work';
const description =
  'How FiberCalc formulas are derived, which Craft Yarn Council sources we cite, AI disclosure, correction log, and changelog for knitting and quilting calculators.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebPage',
      '@id': `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/methodology/#page`,
      name: title,
      description,
      url: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/methodology/`,
      dateModified: `${siteConfig.lastReviewed}T00:00:00+05:00`,
      author: { '@id': CANONICAL_PERSON_ID },
      isPartOf: { '@id': `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/#website` },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/` },
        {
          '@type': 'ListItem',
          position: 2,
          name: 'Methodology',
          item: `${siteConfig.siteUrl}/methodology/`,
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/methodology/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Methodology' }]} />
    <h1>Methodology</h1>
    <p class="meta-row">
      <span>Last reviewed <time datetime={siteConfig.lastReviewed}>{siteConfig.lastReviewed}</time></span>
      <span>Maintainer: <a href="/about/#maintainer">{siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name}</a></span>
    </p>

    <p>
      FiberCalc publishes free, in-browser knitting, crochet, sewing, and quilting calculators. This page explains how
      formulas are chosen, which primary sources we cite, how AI may assist copy (never unchecked math), and where we
      log corrections. Use it when you need provenance—not as a substitute for a pattern’s tested yardage chart.
    </p>

    <h2>How calculations work</h2>
    <p>
      Each calculator documents its formula on the tool page. Yarn estimators use area-based density factors
      calibrated to common pattern yardages and Craft Yarn Council weight categories. Quilt tools use
      perimeter and panel arithmetic. Gauge tools use direct proportion from measured swatches. Unit tests in
      this repository cover the pure math modules.
    </p>

    <h2>Sources policy</h2>
    <p>I cite primary, publicly available standards when a tool depends on them:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.craftyarncouncil.com/standards/yarn-weight-system" rel="noopener noreferrer">CYC Standard Yarn Weight System</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.craftyarncouncil.com/standards/hooks-and-needles" rel="noopener noreferrer">CYC Hooks &amp; Needles</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.craftyarncouncil.com/standards/body-sizing" rel="noopener noreferrer">CYC Body measurements / sizing</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.craftyarncouncil.com/standards/woman-size" rel="noopener noreferrer">CYC Woman size charts</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.sleepproducts.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">International Sleep Products Association</a> (mattress industry context)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Craft “standard” blanket and quilt sizes are community conventions—patterns may differ. I only list a
      source when the page actually uses that data, and I re-check URLs when content changes.
    </p>

    <h2>What the tools leave out</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Dye-lot matching, shrinkage after washing, and highly textured stitch patterns that break averages.</li>
      <li>Longarm quilting fees, batting brand stretch, and directional fabric naps.</li>
      <li>Legal, medical, or professional design advice of any kind.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AI / automation disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Drafts of explanatory copy may be written with AI assistance. Every formula, rate-style constant, and
      reference link is checked by {siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name} against the sources listed on each page
      before publication. Calculator math is implemented in TypeScript with automated tests—not generated at
      request time.
    </p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Correction log</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time> — Removed anonymous “FiberCalc Team” authorship;
        named {siteConfig.defaultAuthor.name} as sole maintainer. Fixed escaped newline characters that
        appeared as visible text between calculator fields. Pointed needle/hook sources at the live CYC
        Hooks &amp; Needles chart.
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-10-23">2026-10-23</time> — SEO/AEO pass: GA module scripts, 308 trailing-slash
        Worker, expanded guides, tool→guide links, site-origin single setting for future custom domain.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changelog">Changelog</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>v{siteConfig.calculatorVersion}</strong> ({siteConfig.launched}) — Initial public release of
        yarn, gauge, sewing, quilting, and reference calculators.
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20">2026-10-20</time> — Mobile SEO / trust pass: PNG Open Graph image,
        TrustBlock sources, mode-aware knitting gauge fields, compact cookie bar, Consent Mode v2 for GA4.
      </li>
      <li>
        <time datetime="2026-10-23">2026-10-23</time> — Guides expanded, new articles, llms.txt inventory,
        per-page OG images, audit guardrails.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Dates</h2>
    <p>
      “Last reviewed” and <code>dateModified</code> change only when formulas, sources, or substantive text
      change—not on routine redeploys. Canonical URLs always use the single <code>PUBLIC_SITE_URL</code>
      setting (documented in the repo as <code>docs/CUSTOM-DOMAIN.md</code>).
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
